(footprint "SW_Kailh_Choc_V2_THT_6.00u_Diode" (version 20221018) (generator pcbnew)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Kailh Choc V2 (PG1353) low profile mechanical keyboard switch, through-hole soldering, single-sided mounting. Plate cut lines: User.1=15.60mm square (cosmetic cover, all switches), User.3=13.95mm square (Kailh Choc V2). Keycap: 6.00u (courtyard 114.25x19.00mm). No stabilizer PCB features. Series diode pads on back side: pad 3 = anode, pad 4 = cathode (cathode bar on B.SilkS, body outline on B.Fab, cathode points up). Combined hand-soldering land for SOD-123 / SOD-323 / MiniMELF (LL-34, LL4148): 2.0x1.4mm pads at +/-1.6mm axial offset. Connect pad 2 to pad 3 (or 1 to 4) externally for the usual row/column matrix.")
  (tags "switch, low_profile, diode")
  (attr through_hole)
